\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sweet is the sunlight after rain,
\par And sweet the sleep which follows
\par pain,
\par And sweetly steals the Sabbath rest
\par Upon the world's work- wearied breast.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Of heaven the sign, of earth the 
\par calm;
\par The poor man's birthright, and his 
\par balm;
\par God's witness of celestial things;
\par A sun with healing in its wings.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. New rising in this gospel time,
\par And in its sevenfold light sublime,
\par Blest day of God! we hail its dawn,
\par To gratitude and worship drawn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O nought of gloom and nought
\par of pride,
\par Should with the sacred hours abide;
\par At work for God, in loved employ,
\par We lose the duty in the joy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Breathe on us, Lord, our sins forgive,
\par And make us strong in faith to live:
\par Our utmost, sorest need supply,
\par And make us strong in faith to die.
\par                                    Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

